    "textWidgets": [
      {
        "widgetId": 2512667,
        "text": "## Sources & Methodology\n\n**Network.** XNET offload and device APIs provide telemetry and device counts. GB in network telemetry and billed GB in the revenue sheet are separate measurements. Device productivity uses the monthly average of operational devices. A deployed device may be awaiting carrier approval before it starts offloading. The current calendar month contains partial data.\n\n**Revenue.** The [XNET revenue sheet](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1NebqJ876SNlO4xPihfJWzsH-V0xzgeA-Qw8i5VcHDU4/edit) provides projected WiFi revenue, payments, transfers and scheduled emissions. Service-month revenue and dated cash receipts are separate. Projected revenue, payments received and transfers can cover different periods. Annualized revenue run rate is an annualization of recent revenue; P/S divides market capitalization by that run rate.\n\n**Market.** DexScreener supplies pool prices, liquidity and rolling 24-hour volume. Price comes from the highest-liquidity XNET-base pool. Market capitalization = price × circulating supply; FDV = price × maximum supply. Provider pool snapshots do not measure guaranteed execution depth.\n\n**Buy & Burn.** Burn charts cover the primary BBB wallet [5Qsy…URzfd](https://solscan.io/account/5QsyByFVJcg7oN76Ma26KEDFQdHt1tsiVExK94zURzfd). The historical unemitted-supply burn is excluded. Latest-burn amount sums burn events in that transaction. Cumulative burn percentage uses the published maximum supply of 1,307,098,713 XNET; the circulating-supply percentage uses the latest circulating supply.\n\n**Emissions.** The XIP-11 schedule allocates 2.5 million XNET per 14-day epoch. Calendar-month totals prorate that rate by the number of days; schedule totals differ from the dates on which tokens are distributed.\n\n**Emissions per GB.** Scheduled monthly XNET emissions ÷ network offload GB, for completed months. The USD series multiplies this ratio by the latest XNET price. It represents emission intensity at today’s price, rather than historical USD payouts or individual deployer earnings.\n\n**Supply & ownership.** Month-end circulation is reconstructed from the September 24, 2026 supply checkpoint and the 61-wallet exclusion list, using transfers and circulating-token burns. Burning tokens from an excluded wallet reduces outstanding supply and the exclusion together, leaving circulation unchanged. Holders are positive-balance owners, not unique people. Bucket lower bounds are inclusive and upper bounds exclusive. Circulating-supply growth is the percentage change from the previous month-end observation; the current month uses its latest available observation.\n\n**Coverage & source status.** Source dates in the freshness table indicate the age of each dataset. Offload/device sources currently retain their last observations while the APIs return HTTP 402. BBB USDC history starts on December 30, 2025. Daily closing balances are carried forward on days without balance changes, followed by current Solana RPC observations. Circulating-supply history starts on September 30, 2024.\n\n[Source catalog](https://github.com/xnet-community-data/xnet-data-integration) · [XNET documentation](https://docs.xnetmobile.com/) · [XNET on DefiLlama](https://defillama.com/protocol/xnet)",
        "position": {
          "col": 0,
          "row": 215,
          "sizeX": 6,
          "sizeY": 23
        }
